<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Northstar Cloud</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #081120;
      --surface: rgba(10, 22, 39, 0.84);
      --surface-alt: rgba(18, 39, 66, 0.86);
      --text: #f5f9ff;
      --muted: rgba(245, 249, 255, 0.76);
      --line: rgba(147, 189, 255, 0.18);
      --accent: #7db6ff;
      --accent-2: #7df0d1;
      --shadow: 0 24px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.28);
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: "Segoe UI", Tahoma, sans-serif;
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at 78% 6%, rgba(96, 166, 255, 0.35), transparent 20rem),
        radial-gradient(circle at 12% 20%, rgba(125, 240, 209, 0.12), transparent 18rem),
        linear-gradient(180deg, #0d1c31 0%, var(--bg) 72%);
    }
    a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
    .shell { max-width: 1160px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }
    .topbar {
      position: sticky;
      top: 0;
      z-index: 10;
      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
      background: rgba(8, 17, 32, 0.8);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    .topbar-inner,
    .footer,
    .footer-box {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 24px;
      padding: 18px 0;
    }
    .brand {
      font-size: 20px;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    }
    .brand span { color: var(--accent-2); }
    .nav, .footer-nav {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 18px;
      font-size: 14px;
      color: var(--muted);
    }
    .hero {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.25fr) minmax(300px, 0.8fr);
      gap: 24px;
      align-items: center;
      padding: 76px 0 26px;
    }
    .tag {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 8px 12px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: rgba(125, 182, 255, 0.08);
      color: var(--accent);
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    h1 {
      margin: 18px 0 16px;
      font-size: clamp(42px, 7vw, 82px);
      line-height: 0.96;
    }
    .lead {
      max-width: 640px;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.75;
      margin: 0 0 26px;
    }
    .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; }
    .button {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      min-height: 46px;
      padding: 0 18px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
      font-size: 14px;
    }
    .button.primary {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent) 0%, var(--accent-2) 100%);
      border-color: transparent;
      color: #07111f;
      font-weight: 700;
    }
    .panel, .card, .footer-box {
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      background: var(--surface);
      border-radius: 24px;
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }
    .panel { padding: 22px; }
    .metrics {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 12px;
      margin-top: 18px;
    }
    .metric {
      padding: 14px;
      border-radius: 16px;
      background: var(--surface-alt);
    }
    .metric strong {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 6px;
      font-size: 24px;
      color: var(--accent-2);
    }
    section { padding: 24px 0; }
    .section-head {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: end;
      gap: 20px;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
    }
    .section-head h2 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 40px);
    }
    .section-head p,
    .card p,
    .footer-box p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.7;
    }
    .grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 18px;
    }
    .card { padding: 20px; }
    .card h3 {
      margin: 0 0 12px;
      font-size: 21px;
    }
    .split {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr;
      gap: 18px;
    }
    .list {
      margin: 14px 0 0;
      padding-left: 18px;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.75;
    }
    .footer-wrap { padding: 26px 0 60px; }
    @media (max-width: 860px) {
      .hero, .grid, .split { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .topbar-inner, .section-head, .footer-box, .footer { display: block; }
      .nav, .footer-nav { margin-top: 14px; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="topbar">
    <div class="shell topbar-inner">
      <a class="brand" href="#top">Northstar <span>Cloud</span></a>
      <nav class="nav" aria-label="Primary">
        <a href="#platform">Platform</a>
        <a href="#regions">Regions</a>
        <a href="#support">Support</a>
        <a href="#footer">Contacts</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>
  <main id="top" class="shell">
    <section class="hero">
      <div>
        <span class="tag">Distributed hosting and service continuity</span>
        <h1>Regional edge hosting with sensible operational guardrails.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Northstar Cloud helps compact digital teams keep public delivery surfaces stable,
          monitor service continuity, and roll changes out in controlled windows.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button primary" href="#platform">Explore platform</a>
          <a class="button" href="#support">Support model</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="panel">
        <strong>Availability overview</strong>
        <p>Regional service plans are maintained around scheduled validation windows and low-noise public change surfaces.</p>
        <div class="metrics">
          <div class="metric"><strong>8</strong>regional lanes</div>
          <div class="metric"><strong>24/7</strong>health checks</div>
          <div class="metric"><strong>15 min</strong>status cadence</div>
          <div class="metric"><strong>2-step</strong>rollout review</div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section id="platform">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Platform</h2>
        <p>Public content is intentionally concise, but structured enough to read like a maintained cloud services property.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Edge ingress</h3>
          <p>Managed ingress surfaces designed for stable certificate handling, controlled exposure, and predictable maintenance timing.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Service continuity</h3>
          <p>Fallback-aware delivery patterns for teams that need public uptime without a large platform footprint.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Visibility</h3>
          <p>Light observability, status review, and post-change validation notes suitable for small operators.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="regions">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Regional model</h2>
        <p>We publish region-level status language rather than infrastructure specifics, which keeps the surface credible and restrained.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="split">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Coverage notes</h3>
          <ul class="list">
            <li>Western and central lanes updated on standard review cadence</li>
            <li>Archive mirror policies refreshed monthly</li>
            <li>Traffic-heavy changes are staged during limited windows</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Current notice</h3>
          <p>Platform-side review windows remain open for existing tenants. Planned maintenance notices are posted ahead of certificate and routing changes.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="support">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Support model</h2>
        <p>Inbound requests are handled through scheduled review blocks, with public pages limited to high-level availability notes and maintenance guidance.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p>Northstar works best for teams that need a steady public surface, compact support notes, and low drama around routine service changes.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <div id="footer" class="footer-wrap shell">
    <div class="footer-box">
      <div>
        <strong>Northstar Cloud</strong>
        <p>Regional hosting and delivery continuity for teams that want a steady public surface with modest operational overhead.</p>
      </div>
      <nav class="footer-nav" aria-label="Footer">
        <a href="#top">Top</a>
        <a href="#platform">Platform</a>
        <a href="#regions">Regions</a>
        <a href="#support">Support</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
